language sdl-mvp1-exercise version 0.1.

data-type IdentityValue.
data-type RevisionValue.
data-type QualityValue.
data-type LengthValue.
data-type DecimalValue.
data-type TextValue.
data-type ActionValue.
data-type StateRecord.
data-type ProfileSampleValue.
data-type SeriesValue.
data-type MatrixValue.
data-type ListValue.
data-type SchemaValue.
data-type StopOccurrenceValue.
data-type ProductionRecordValue.

IdentityValue describes "Stable opaque identity, not interchangeable merely because two IDs use strings.".
RevisionValue describes "Monotonic within explicitly identified owner/session; no universal global revision.".
QualityValue describes "Valid/unknown/unavailable/stale/invalid/pending are distinct; actual wire enum mapping is contract-specific.".
LengthValue describes "Quantity length; source contract defines actual unit, e.g. Machine v1 cm; display conversion is explicit.".
DecimalValue describes "Numeric value with domain precision/rounding policy still to be bound where unspecified.".
TextValue describes "Text content; human labels are not semantic identity.".
ActionValue describes "Typed intent plus availability; does not itself grant server control authority.".
StateRecord describes "Composite owner state whose complete member schema must be supplied before execution.".
ProfileSampleValue describes "Coherent profile identity/revision, position, diameter and quality from domain owner.".
SeriesValue describes "Ordered/indexed stable samples with append/patch semantics; collection revision differs from view revision.".
MatrixValue describes "Semantic row/column identities, value type and matrix revision; visual order is not cell identity.".
ListValue describes "Independent stable entries; reorder does not recreate entry identity.".
SchemaValue describes "Presentation node/binding/compatibility schema with structural revision; no executable callbacks.".
StopOccurrenceValue describes "Session-qualified stop_id, semantic payload and advertised retention, distinct from command_id.".
ProductionRecordValue describes "Durable cut-time provenance and domain fact, not optional Lab history.".
ProfileSampleValue field "profileId" as IdentityValue.
ProfileSampleValue field "revision" as RevisionValue.
ProfileSampleValue field "position" as LengthValue.
ProfileSampleValue field "diameter" as LengthValue.
ProfileSampleValue field "quality" as QualityValue.
ProductionRecordValue field "recordId" as IdentityValue.
ProductionRecordValue field "calibrationRevision" as RevisionValue.
ProductionRecordValue field "policyRevision" as RevisionValue.
ProductionRecordValue field "economicRevision" as RevisionValue.
ProductionRecordValue field "aptSourceId" as IdentityValue.
ProductionRecordValue field "modelId" as IdentityValue.
ProductionRecordValue field "planRevision" as RevisionValue.
